.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-DELETE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-delete - Delete a team


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team delete <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a team

.PP
Delete a team after exact confirmation and a matching generation. This affects team ownership and grants; inspect attached resources and enrolled team machines first.

.PP
Teams use explicit membership and resource grants. Membership alone does not grant machine use, ENV values, previews, or tunnels. Mutations use the current team generation to reject stale edits; read pb team get before retrying a conflicting change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	exact team identifier

.PP
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for delete

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
